Package: reconf
Title: Confidence Intervals for Random Effect Parameters in Linear Mixed Models
Version: 0.1.1
Authors@R: c(
    person("Karl Oskar", "Ekvall", email = "k.o.ekvall@gmail.com",
    role = c("aut", "cre")),
    person("Yiqiao", "Zhang", email = "yiqiaozhang@ufl.edu", role = "aut"),
    person("Matias", "Shedden", email = "sheddenmatias@ufl.edu", role = "ctb"))
Description: Computes score-based confidence intervals and hypothesis tests
    for variance and covariance parameters of random effects in linear mixed
    models fitted with 'lme4'. The intervals invert the efficient score test
    on the natural variance-covariance scale and are designed to remain
    valid near the boundary of the parameter space, where Wald and likelihood
    ratio intervals can be unreliable. The methods are described in Shedden and 
    Ekvall (2026, in preparation), building on Ekvall and Bottai (2026)
    <doi:10.1093/biomet/asaf079>, Zhang, Ekvall, and Molstad (2025)
    <doi:10.1093/biomet/asaf010>, and Ekvall and Bottai (2022)
    <doi:10.1214/22-AOS2177>.
URL: https://github.com/koekvall/reconf
BugReports: https://github.com/koekvall/reconf/issues
